    </h1>

    <p class="policy-updated">
      Last updated: September 14, 2026
    </p>


    <section>

      <h2>About this policy</h2>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ is an Android application developed
        by Last Day Software for organizing and tracking movies
        and television shows.
      </p>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ is designed to work locally on your
        device without requiring an account.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ stores information locally so that
        your Library and tracking history remain available
        even when you are offline or signed out.
      </p>

      <p>
        Local data may include:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Library membership</li>
        <li>Movie watch counts</li>
        <li>TV-show and episode tracking</li>
        <li>Favorites and archived state</li>
        <li>User preferences</li>
        <li>Notification and synchronization preferences</li>
        <li>Cached TMDB metadata and artwork references</li>
      </ul>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Optional Google sign-in</h2>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ offers optional Google sign-in.
        Authentication is provided through Google OAuth
        and Supabase authentication.
      </p>

      <p>
        An account is not required to use the local Library.
      </p>

      <p>
        Authentication tokens are stored locally using
        Android Keystore-backed encryption and are excluded
        from Android backup.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Cloud Backup</h2>

      <p>
        Cloud Backup v1 is manual. Series Organizer+ does not
        automatically upload your Library merely because you
        sign in.
      </p>

      <p>
        When you explicitly request a cloud backup, the backup
        may contain:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Library membership</li>
        <li>Movie tracking</li>
        <li>TV-show tracking</li>
        <li>Episode tracking</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Cloud backups do not contain:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>TMDB metadata or caches</li>
        <li>Person data</li>
        <li>Posters or other artwork</li>
        <li>Analytics preferences</li>
        <li>General app or device preferences</li>
        <li>Notification permissions or schedules</li>
        <li>Authentication tokens</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The cloud-backup service retains at most the five
        newest immutable backup snapshots associated with
        an account.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Optional analytics</h2>

      <p>
        Firebase Analytics is disabled by default.
        Analytics collection is enabled only after explicit
        user opt-in.
      </p>

      <p>
        When enabled, analytics may include:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>A pseudonymous app-instance identifier</li>
        <li>Application lifecycle and session activity</li>
        <li>Coarse geographical information</li>
        <li>Device and platform information</li>
        <li>Aggregate Library movie and TV-show counts</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ does not send media titles,
        search text, biographies, email addresses,
        authentication tokens or individual watch-history
        records to Firebase Analytics.
      </p>

      <p>
        Advertising identifiers and advertising
        personalization are disabled.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Services used by Series Organizer+</h2>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ communicates with third-party
        services when required for specific application
        features.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>TMDB</strong> — movie, TV, episode,
          Person, artwork, video and provider metadata.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>JustWatch</strong> — streaming-availability
          attribution supplied through TMDB.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — optional authentication
          and cloud backup.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Google OAuth</strong> — optional Google sign-in.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Google / Firebase</strong> — optional
          analytics when explicitly enabled.
        </li>
      </ul>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Data location and transmission</h2>

      <p>
        The current Supabase backend used for optional account
        and cloud-backup functionality is hosted in the
        EU West region.
      </p>

      <p>
        Network communication with supported services is
        performed using encrypted HTTPS connections.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some third-party services may process information
        outside the user's country or region according to
        their own infrastructure and privacy policies.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>

      <p>
        Local application data remains on the device until it
        is removed through application functionality, cleared
        through Android settings, or removed by uninstalling
        the application, subject to Android platform behavior.
      </p>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ cloud backup stores at most the five
        newest backup snapshots associated with an account.
      </p>

      <p>
        Deleting the Series Organizer+ cloud account removes
        the account and its associated cloud-backup snapshots.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>

      <p>
        You may:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Use Series Organizer+ without signing in</li>
        <li>Choose whether to create a cloud backup</li>
        <li>Choose whether optional analytics are enabled</li>
        <li>Sign out of your Google-linked account</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your cloud account and backups</li>
      </ul>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Account deletion</h2>

      <p>
        Instructions for deleting a Series Organizer+ cloud
        account are available on the
        <a href="account-deletion.html">
          Account deletion page
        </a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Account deletion affects the Series Organizer+ cloud
        account and cloud backups. It does not delete the
        user's Google Account.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Children</h2>

      <p>
        Series Organizer+ is not specifically designed as a
        children's service.
      </p>

      <p class="policy-note">
        The developer must confirm the intended minimum-age
        positioning and any additional wording required before
        publication.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated when Series Organizer+
        changes or when its services and data-handling practices
        change.
      </p>

      <p>
        The latest version will be published on this page with
        an updated revision date.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Privacy and support contact information will be added
        here once the public Last Day Software support address
        has been confirmed.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section class="policy-needed">

      <h2>Information needed from the developer</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Public support/privacy email address</li>
        <li>Intended age/minimum-age positioning</li>
        <li>Any legally required retention exceptions</li>
      </ul>

    </section>

